  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 146 AM MDT Mon Aug 10 2026\n\nThe leading edge of monsoon moisture will be over the southern \nhighlands today. Expect another round of isolated thunderstorms \nthis afternoon there. Otherwise, warm and breezy conditions are \nlikely today with gusts of 20 to 30 mph common across much of \nthe region. Highs today will be in the low to mid 90s for many \nof our valley communities. \n\nAnother round of isolated thunderstorms across the southern \nhighlands is possible Tuesday afternoon. High temps look slightly \ncooler with more clouds expected across the region. The bigger push \nof moisture doesn't arrive until Tuesday Night into Wednesday. With \na fair amount of clouds around on Wednesday, highs will probably \nstay in the mid to upper 80s. Although we may have too much clouds \nfor much thunderstorm development.\n\nThursday looks very active as a trough pushes into the region. \nScattered thunderstorms is expected and some of those storms could \nproduce some heavy rainfall. We remain in the southwesterly monsoon \nflow into Friday. Debatable of how much storm coverage we actually \nhave on Friday with quite a bit of moisture moving through the \nregion. Still, the threat for heavy rain from thunderstorms exists \nif we can get storms to develop.",
